## Phase 1 — Backend: Express + TypeScript + Prisma Setup
**Commit:** `chore(backend): express + typescript + prisma scaffold with sqlite schema`

- [ ] Init `backend/` as a Node.js TypeScript project (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`)
- [ ] Install dependencies: `express`, `cors`, `dotenv`, `@prisma/client`, `zod`
- [ ] Install dev dependencies: `typescript`, `ts-node`, `nodemon`, `prisma`, `jest`, `supertest`, `@types/*`
- [ ] Create `backend/src/app.ts` — Express app with CORS, JSON middleware, health route
- [ ] Create `backend/src/server.ts` — entry point (listens on PORT)
- [ ] Create `backend/src/lib/prisma.ts` — Prisma singleton
- [ ] Define `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`:
  - `Employee` model (id, employeeId, name, email, country, department, role, salary, currency, employmentType, status, hireDate, createdAt, updatedAt)
  - `ExchangeRate` model (id, currency, rateToUsd, effectiveDate)
- [ ] Run `prisma migrate dev --name init` to generate SQLite DB
- [ ] Verify `GET /api/health` returns `{ status: "ok" }`
- [ ] Add `npm run dev`, `npm run build`, `npm start` scripts

